.TH PSPP 1 "2026-11-12" "pspp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pspp \- interactive and scriptable process memory viewer grouped by parent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pspp
.RB [ \-\-mem
.IR KIND ]
.RB [ \-\-agg
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-\-sort
.IR FIELD ]
.RB [ \-r | \-\-reverse ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-base10 ]
.RB [ \-\-update\-ms
.IR MS ]
.br
.B pspp
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATTERN ]
.br
.B pspp \-\-query
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pspp
("ps plus plus") sums memory used by running processes grouped by their parent
process
.RI ( "pid <- ppid" ),
exposing the true memory footprint of multi-process applications such as
browsers, WebView/Electron apps, build tools, and worker supervisors.
.PP
When invoked on an interactive terminal with no query-mode arguments,
.B pspp
opens a live, mouse-enabled terminal interface inspired by
.BR btop (1)
with braille memory history graphs, a grass-green to bloody-red usage gradient,
and an expandable process tree.
When
.IR PATTERN ,
.BR \-\-pid ,
.BR \-\-min ,
.BR \-\-top ,
.B \-\-json
or
.B \-\-query
is provided\(emor when standard output is piped or redirected\(em\fBpspp\fR
runs a single snapshot in non-interactive query mode, prints a plain table or
JSON document to standard output, and exits.
Query mode is deterministic: it never reads
.IR pspp.conf ;
its defaults are
.BR "\-\-mem rss" ,
.BR "\-\-agg rollup" ,
.BR "\-\-sort agg"
and binary units.
The plain header
.RB ( "RSS \(*S (rollup)" )
and the JSON output name the mode in effect.
.PP
.BR \-\-mem ,
.BR \-\-agg ,
.BR \-\-sort ,
.BR \-r / \-\-reverse ,
.B \-\-base10
and
.B \-\-update\-ms
apply to whichever mode runs.
In the TUI they override
.I pspp.conf
for that run only and are never saved; with
.B save_on_exit
enabled, only settings changed inside the TUI are written (and turning
.B save_on_exit
off in Options persists
.B "save_on_exit = false"
without saving other transient session changes).
.SS Aggregation Modes
.TP
.B rollup
Sums each process together with all of its descendants (children,
grandchildren, and deeper).
Default in both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.B flat
Sums only direct children under each parent process, keeping parent and child
layers separate.
.PP
In query mode, the final
.B TOTAL
row (and JSON
.BR total )
counts every process covered by the returned rows at most once: in
.B rollup
mode, rows that already have an ancestor in the returned set are not added a
second time.
.SS Memory Metrics and Approximate Values
Depending on the platform,
.B pspp
supports:
.TP
.B rss
Resident Set Size: RAM the process is using right now, including shared pages
also mapped by other processes (macOS and Linux; default).
.TP
.B vsz
Virtual Size: total virtual address space reserved by the process, most of
which is not backed by physical RAM (macOS and Linux).
.TP
.B footprint
Apple's physical footprint
.RI ( ri_phys_footprint
via
.BR proc_pid_rusage ),
matching Activity Monitor's Memory column (macOS only).
.TP
.B pss
Proportional Set Size from
.IR /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup :
RAM used with shared pages divided evenly across sharing processes (Linux
only).
.TP
.B uss
Unique Set Size
.RI ( "Private_Clean + Private_Dirty" ):
RAM private to a single process\(emroughly what killing it frees immediately
(Linux only).
.TP
.B swap
Swapped-out bytes reported by
.I /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup
(Linux only).
.PP
When per-process privileged metrics are unreadable without elevated permissions,
.B pspp
keeps the process in the snapshot, reports its own value as
.B "0 B~"
and appends a trailing tilde
.RB ( ~ )
to any ancestor sum that includes it.
On macOS,
.B sysctl(KERN_PROC_ALL)
preserves the full
.I "pid <- ppid"
hierarchy without root privileges, while unreadable per-process memory counters
.RB ( rss ,
.BR vsz ,
and
.B footprint
on other users' or system processes) report
.B "0 B~"
and mark ancestor sums approximate
.RB ( ~ )
unless run with
.BR sudo (8).
On Linux,
.B rss
and
.B vsz
are read from
.IR /proc/<pid>/stat ,
while unreadable
.I /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup
counters
.RB ( pss ,
.BR uss ,
.BR swap )
likewise report
.B "0 B~"
and mark ancestor sums approximate
.RB ( ~ ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATTERN
Case-insensitive substring filter matched against process command names
.RB ( COMM ).
Triggers non-interactive query mode.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-f / \-\-filter
(passing both is a usage error and exits with status
.BR 2 ).
Regex-style
.B !
prefixes are not currently supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid " PID"
Restrict query output to
.I PID
and its descendant subtree.
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-mem " KIND"
Select memory metric:
.BR rss ,
.BR vsz ,
.B footprint
(macOS), or
.BR pss ,
.BR uss ,
.B swap
(Linux).
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-agg " MODE"
Select aggregation mode:
.B rollup
or
.BR flat .
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-min " SIZE"
Filter out rows whose aggregated memory is below
.IR SIZE .
Accepts byte integers or binary unit suffixes (case-insensitive):
.BR B ,
.BR K / KB / KiB ,
.BR M / MB / MiB ,
.BR G / GB / GiB ,
.BR T / TB / TiB ,
.BR P / PB / PiB
(for example,
.BR 512K ,
.BR 100M ,
.BR 1.5G ).
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " FIELD"
Sort rows by
.B agg
(aggregated memory; default descending),
.B own
(own memory; default descending),
.B pid
(default ascending), or
.B comm
(case-insensitive; default ascending).
Ties break by ascending PID.
Applies to both TUI and query mode (in the TUI, overrides
.B sort_key
and uses its natural default direction unless
.BR \-r / \-\-reverse
is also passed).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reverse
Invert the sort direction in both TUI and query mode: reverses the natural
direction of
.B \-\-sort
.RB ( agg / own
ascending;
.BR pid / comm
descending), or inverts
.B sort_reverse
from
.I pspp.conf
when
.B \-\-sort
is omitted in the TUI.
Does not force query mode on its own.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Show at most
.I N
rows after sorting
.RI ( N
must be at least 1).
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Format query output as pretty-printed JSON
.RB ( "{ ""mem"": ""rss"", ""agg"": ""rollup"", ""rows"": [...], ""total"": <bytes>, ""total_approximate"": <bool> }" )
with raw integer byte values.
Each element of
.B rows
contains
.BR pid ,
.BR ppid ,
.BR comm ,
.BR own ,
.BR own_approximate ,
.BR agg ,
.B pct
(aggregated memory as a percentage of total RAM, one decimal),
.BR children ,
.BR descendants ,
and
.BR approximate .
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.B \-\-query
Force one-shot query mode even when standard output is a terminal.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-filter " TEXT
Pre-set the TUI process filter (like
.BR "btop \-f" ).
In query mode it is used as
.I PATTERN
when none is given; passing both
.I PATTERN
and
.BR \-f / \-\-filter
is a usage error (exit
.BR 2 ).
.TP
.B \-\-base10
Format human-readable sizes using decimal powers of 1000
.RB ( KB / MB / GB )
instead of binary powers of 1024
.RB ( KiB / MiB / GiB ).
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-update\-ms " MS"
Refresh interval in milliseconds for interactive TUI mode, clamped to
.BR 100 .. 86400000
(default:
.BR 2000 ,
or
.B update_ms
from
.IR pspp.conf ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print short
.RB ( \-h )
or detailed
.RB ( \-\-help )
usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
The interactive TUI supports keyboard control across all views and overlays:
.\" BEGIN GENERATED: key-bindings
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B Up/Down, j/k
Move selection one row (j/k need vim_keys).
.TP
.B PgUp/PgDn
Move by one page.
.TP
.B Home/End, g/G
Jump to first/last row (g/G need vim_keys).
.TP
.B h, ?, F1
Open Help (h always opens Help, even with vim_keys off).
.TP
.B o, F2
Open Options.
.TP
.B + / \-
Increase / decrease the refresh interval by 100 ms.
.TP
.B m vs btop
m cycles the memory type here; btop uses m for its menu (pspp's menu is
Esc).
.TP
.B q/Q, Ctrl\-C, Ctrl\-Q
Quit pspp (Ctrl\-C/Ctrl\-Q from any mode).
.TP
.B f/F or /
Start filter input.
.TP
.B c/C
Clear the committed filter.
.TP
.B Esc
Open main menu.
.SS Tree
.TP
.B Space or Enter
Toggle expand/collapse on selected node (also while filtering).
.TP
.B Left
Collapse selected node, or select parent.
.TP
.B Right, l
Expand selected node (l needs vim_keys).
.TP
.B z / [
Collapse all non\-root subtrees (again: roots too).
.TP
.B Z / ]
Expand all nodes.
.SS Display & Filter
.TP
.B e/E
Toggle aggregation mode: rollup/flat.
.TP
.B m/M
Cycle memory type.
.TP
.B s
Cycle sort key.
.TP
.B S or r/R
Reverse sort direction.
.TP
.B Filter input
Type any characters (including spaces) to filter live and expand match
ancestors.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete one character in filter input.
.TP
.B Delete / Ctrl\-U
Clear the filter input.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-W
Delete previous word in filter input.
.TP
.B Enter
Keep the filter and return to the table.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel filter edit and restore the prior filter and tree.
.SS Menu / Overlays
.TP
.B Menu: Up/Down, j/k, Tab
Select Options / Help / Quit.
.TP
.B Menu: Enter/Space
Activate selected menu button.
.TP
.B Menu: Esc/q/Q
Close menu.
.TP
.B Options: Up/Down, j/k
