.SH EXIT STATUS
In query mode,
.B pspp
uses
.BR grep (1)-style
exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
At least one matching row was printed (an early closed pipe on stdout, such as
.BR "pspp | head" ,
also exits 0).
In TUI mode, clean exit returns 0.
.TP
.B 1
Query matched zero rows (plain mode also prints
.B "no matches"
to standard error;
.B \-\-json
prints
.BR "{""mem"":""rss"",""agg"":""rollup"",""rows"":[],""total"":0,""total_approximate"":false}" ).
In TUI mode, terminal initialization/runtime failure returns 1.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (invalid option, conflicting
.I PATTERN
and
.BR \-f / \-\-filter ,
unknown/unavailable
.BR \-\-mem ,
bad
.B \-\-min
size, or
.BR "\-\-top 0" )
or standard output write error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables ANSI colours in the TUI, selects
.B tty
graph glyphs, renders ASCII
.BR # / \-
usage meters and square box borders, and uses reverse-video selection
highlights without modifying
.IR pspp.conf .
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Consulted when
.B truecolor
is
.BR auto :
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
enables 24-bit RGB gradients; otherwise
.B pspp
falls back to the 256-colour palette.
.TP
.B TERM
Consulted when
.B graph_symbol
is
.B auto
(selects
.B tty
glyphs for
.BR linux ,
.BR dumb ,
or a
.B TERM
without
.B color
when
.B COLORTERM
is unset).
.TP
.B PSPP_CONFIG_DIR
When set and non-empty, overrides the directory used for
.I pspp.conf
and
.IR themes/ .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used on Linux to locate
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pspp/pspp.conf
when
.B PSPP_CONFIG_DIR
is unset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PSPP_CONFIG_DIR/pspp.conf
Overrides the default configuration file location when
.B PSPP_CONFIG_DIR
is set and non-empty.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pspp/pspp.conf
Default TOML configuration file on Linux (or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pspp/pspp.conf ).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/pspp/pspp.conf
Default TOML configuration file on macOS (via platform config directory lookup).
.PP
Supported TOML keys:
.BR update_ms ,
.BR mem_kind ,
.BR agg_mode ,
.BR graph_symbol ,
.BR base10 ,
.BR save_on_exit ,
.BR sort_key ,
.BR sort_reverse ,
.BR color_theme ,
.BR theme_background ,
.BR truecolor " (auto|on|off)" ,
.BR rounded_corners ,
.BR vim_keys ,
.BR disable_mouse ,
.BR clock_format " (strftime; empty hides the clock)" ,
.BR background_update ,
and
.BR force_tty .
All are editable live in the Options overlay.
Enabling
.B force_tty
forces 16-colour ANSI TTY mode: ASCII
.BR # / \-
meters,
.B tty
graph glyphs, and square borders, overriding
.BR graph_symbol ,
.BR rounded_corners ,
.BR truecolor ,
and custom
.I .theme
files.
.TP
.I $PSPP_CONFIG_DIR/themes/NAME.theme
btop-format theme files selectable through
.BR color_theme .
Recognised keys:
.BR main_bg ,
.BR main_fg ,
.BR title ,
.BR hi_fg ,
.BR selected_bg ,
.BR selected_fg ,
.BR inactive_fg ,
.BR meter_bg ,
.BR div_line ,
and the usage gradient
.BR cpu_start / cpu_mid / cpu_end ;
other keys are ignored.
Without
.BR PSPP_CONFIG_DIR ,
the directory is
.I themes/
next to
.IR pspp.conf .
.PP
When
.B save_on_exit
is
.B true
(default), TUI option changes are saved atomically via a temporary sibling file
on exit; toggling
.B save_on_exit
off in Options writes
.B "save_on_exit = false"
without saving other transient session edits.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch the interactive TUI with default settings:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print the top 5 process subtrees by Resident Set Size:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-top 5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find processes matching "chrome" whose subtree uses at least 200 MiB:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp chrome \-\-min 200M
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect direct-child memory on macOS using physical footprint:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-mem footprint \-\-agg flat \-\-top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sort query output alphabetically by command name in reverse
.RI ( "Z -> A" ):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-query \-\-sort comm \-r \-\-top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit JSON for a specific PID subtree and extract total bytes with
.BR jq (1):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-pid 1 \-\-json | jq '{total, total_approximate}'
.fi
.RE
